{"step_index":49,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:36:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-21T16:06:58+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-21T16:06:59+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/renu5/Downloads/priyanshu%20readme/knowledge/workflow_and_schedule.md`\nTotal Lines: 28\nTotal Bytes: 1203\nShowing lines 1 to 28\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Workflow and Schedule\n2: \n3: ## Your Role (Agent)\n4: Mentor and manager. Track progress, call out slacking, give NEXT 1-2 actions only.\n5: \n6: **Workflow Order:**\n7: 1. Stickman scripts FIRST\n8: 2. Study Nishchay competitor scripts (parallel)\n9: 3. Nishchay production AFTER study phase\n10: 4. Clipping — ongoing, lower priority\n11: \n12: ## Communication Rules\n13: - Anti-sycophancy always active. No empty praise.\n14: - Prefix with \"Priyanshu,\" — answer first, then reasoning.\n15: - Density over length. Outcomes over process. Specificity required.\n16: - Challenge bad ideas before execution. Catch bluffs.\n17: - Vague requests get questions. Fast iteration — executable version first.\n18: - Script = most important thing for both channels. AI as edge, not crutch.\n19: - Daily update protocol: acknowledge → check against plan → give next 1-2 actions → call out if off-track.\n20: \n21: ## Schedule\n22: - **Home:** 9-11 AM (light tasks)\n23: - **Library:** 12-6:45 PM (MAIN — all heavy work)\n24: - **Gym:** 7-10 PM (NotebookLM audio + voice notes)\n25: - **Light work:** 10 PM-12 AM\n26: - **Thursday:** college + REST. 6 days/week. 80% YouTube, 20% clipping.\n27: - **⚠️ DEADLINE: Feb 1, 2027** — Monetization threshold doubles (4K→8K watch hours). Apply ASAP if near threshold.\n28: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":50,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:36:59Z","content":"Good. I'll save these in two places:\n\n1. **Audiobook idea** → `knowledge/channels.md` — new \"Under Evaluation\" section\n2. **Thumbnail workflow** → `knowledge/thumbnail_workflow.md` — new enforced rule file\n\nThen update `CONTEXT.md` and `priyanshu-agent.md` so any new conversation picks both up.","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":"false","Description":"\"Added the audiobook channel idea as a new 'Under Evaluation' section so future conversations know about this research in progress.\"","EndLine":"20","Instruction":"\"Add new section for audiobook channel idea under evaluation, before Dismissed section\"","ReplacementContent":"\"## Clipping (Side)\\n- Whop + Vyro. Details in `clipping/` folder.\\n- Lower priority, editing practice.\\n\\n## Audiobook / Book Summary Channel (Under Evaluation — Sept 2026)\\n- **Status:** Research phase. NOT started. Evaluating viability before committing.\\n- **Concept:** Book summaries (public domain classics + popular copyrighted bestsellers). 45 min to 3 hours per video.\\n- **Languages:** Testing both Hindi and English to see which grows faster.\\n- **Format:** AI voiceover + simple visuals (captions over images/whiteboard/static backgrounds). ~90% AI production, manual script QC only.\\n- **Monetization:** AdSense + book affiliate links + sponsorships. Spotify audio distribution if YouTube works.\\n- **Key question:** Can minimal-effort format (AI voice + captions on images) survive YouTube's Inauthentic Content policy and get monetized?\\n- **Inspiration channels:** @SoulArcStudios, @LifeUpgrade27, @AudiobooksArc, @SwaroopSinghRajput, @Antidote_thechannel, @Elite_Audiobooks, @EnglishAvenuee\\n- **EnglishAvenuee insight:** Human-made channel (NOT AI) with dead-simple format (real voiceover + captions on background). Earns ~$15k/month. Proves minimal production can earn big if content carries the value.\\n- **Research prompt:** Saved in artifact `audiobook_niche_prompt_review.md` — 8-question prompt for vidIQ AI Coach covering viability, monetization risk, RPM, copyright, Hindi vs English, top channels, format replicability, and alternative niches with same simple format.\\n- **Next step:** Paste prompt into vidIQ AI Coach → verify channel monetization with NexLev → bring data back for final verdict.\\n- **Risk notes:** See `cash_cow_channels_and_mitigation.md` artifact for full risk analysis of faceless/AI channels in 2026.\\n\\n## Dismissed\\n- Any other channel visible in screenshots = burner, ignore.\\n\"","StartLine":"14","TargetContent":"\"## Clipping (Side)\\n- Whop + Vyro. Details in `clipping/` folder.\\n- Lower priority, editing practice.\\n\\n## Dismissed\\n- Any other channel visible in screenshots = burner, ignore.\\n\"","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\priyanshu readme\\\\knowledge\\\\channels.md\"","toolAction":"\"Saving audiobook idea\"","toolSummary":"\"Channels file update\""}}]}
