{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:37:27Z","content":"Now let me create the thumbnail workflow as an enforced rule:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Thumbnail Generation Workflow (ENFORCED — Non-Negotiable)\\n\\n**Added:** 2026-09-21\\n**Applies to:** ALL channels, ALL videos, ANY time thumbnails are discussed.\\n\\n## Rule: Outlier-First Thumbnail Design\\n\\nWhenever Priyanshu asks to create, design, or generate a thumbnail for ANY video topic, this workflow is MANDATORY. Do NOT skip steps. Do NOT jump straight to generating a thumbnail.\\n\\n### Step 1: Find Outlier Videos (vidIQ)\\n- Use vidIQ's outlier search to find all outlier videos on the SAME TOPIC (not same title — same topic).\\n- Cast a wide net: include different title variations, angles, and phrasings of the topic.\\n- Collect at least 5-10 outlier videos.\\n\\n### Step 2: Extract & Analyze Their Thumbnails (vidIQ)\\n- Use vidIQ's `similar_thumbnails` or manual extraction to pull every outlier video's thumbnail.\\n- For EACH thumbnail, reverse-engineer and document:\\n  - **Composition:** Layout, focal point, rule of thirds, whitespace usage.\\n  - **Colors:** Dominant palette, contrast strategy, background color.\\n  - **Text:** What text is on the thumbnail (if any), font style, size, placement.\\n  - **Faces/Emotions:** Any faces shown, what emotion, eye direction.\\n  - **Objects/Props:** Key visual elements, scale, positioning.\\n  - **Curiosity trigger:** What makes a viewer NEED to click? What's the visual hook?\\n  - **What's deliberately hidden/cropped:** What is NOT shown that creates curiosity?\\n\\n### Step 3: Compile the Reverse-Engineering Data\\n- Create a structured summary of ALL analyzed thumbnails.\\n- Identify common patterns across the top performers.\\n- Identify what's DIFFERENT about the #1 outlier vs the rest.\\n- Note any anti-patterns (things all outlier thumbnails avoid).\\n\\n### Step 4: Generate Thumbnail Concepts\\n- Use the compiled data to generate 3-5 thumbnail concepts that:\\n  - Incorporate the winning patterns from outlier analysis.\\n  - Fix weaknesses found in existing outlier thumbnails.\\n  - Are BETTER than every thumbnail analyzed — not copies, improvements.\\n- Each concept mu\n<truncated 938 bytes>","Description":"\"Enforced thumbnail workflow rule: always start by finding outlier videos via vidIQ, reverse-engineering their thumbnails, then creating something better. This is a non-negotiable production rule.\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\priyanshu readme\\\\knowledge\\\\thumbnail_workflow.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating thumbnail rule\"","toolSummary":"\"Thumbnail workflow file\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
