{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:52:45Z","content":"Now create the risk notes file:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Risk Notes — Audiobook / Book Summary Channel\\n# Created: Sept 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## YouTube Policy Risks (2025-2026)\\n\\n### 1. Inauthentic Content Policy (Replaced \\\"Repetitious Content\\\" — July 2025)\\n- YouTube now flags content created strictly to harvest views without meaningful human creative input\\n- Covers: rigid template workflows, mass-produced AI slop, no original analysis\\n- Stock footage + generic voiceover = NOT transformative\\n- **Your risk level:** MEDIUM — AI voice + captions on images is very simple. Must have strong script quality and human QC to pass.\\n\\n### 2. Mandatory AI Disclosure\\n- Must check \\\"Altered or Synthetic Content\\\" box for AI voice, AI images, AI video\\n- YouTube runs multimodal classifiers to detect undisclosed AI content\\n- Repeated non-disclosure = strikes, algorithmic suppression, YPP removal\\n- **Your risk level:** LOW — just check the box every time. Zero cost.\\n\\n### 3. Feb 1, 2027 — Monetization Threshold Doubles\\n- Watch hours: 4,000 → 8,000 in previous 365 days\\n- Shorts views: 10M → 20M in previous 90 days\\n- Subscribers: stays at 1,000\\n- Grandfathering: existing YPP partners before Feb 1, 2027 stay in\\n- **Your risk level:** HIGH — if this channel is a secondary project, you likely won't hit threshold before deadline. Will face 8,000-hour requirement.\\n\\n### 4. Algorithm Satisfaction Weighting\\n- YouTube now weights satisfaction signals (post-watch surveys, \\\"Not Interested\\\" rates, repeat viewership)\\n- Frame-by-frame AI analysis of pacing, visual redundancy, tone\\n- Generic stock loops and repetitive AI pacing get suppressed\\n- **Your risk level:** MEDIUM — long-form audiobook content naturally has high watch time if content is good. But AI pacing could be detected.\\n\\n### 5. Market Saturation\\n- AI tools lowered barrier to zero. Millions of low-quality faceless channels flooded every niche 2023-2025\\n- Impression pools diluted, CPMs plummeted for generic faceless content\\n- Advertisers blacklist channels showing signs of automated content\\n- **Yo\n<truncated 2617 bytes>","Description":"\"Risk analysis for the audiobook channel — YouTube policy risks, copyright risks, niches to avoid, and mitigation strategies. Separated from the implementation plan to keep it clean.\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\priyanshu readme\\\\youtube\\\\Audiobook Book Summary\\\\risk_notes.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating risk notes\"","toolSummary":"\"Risk notes file\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
